title An index is not a teacher
rota lap 4326, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; law and boundary. The boundary this lap needed was which pages genuinely want Bhakta, and it cut through my own recommendation.
think My closing line last lap named three next leaves: edu, study and demos. Air asks where each thing ends, so I read all three before touching any.
obs MY OWN RECOMMEND WAS WRONG AND THE ROOM SAID SO IN ITS FIRST LINE. edu/README.md opens `This room is an index rather than a shelf`. An index answers WHERE DOES THAT LIVE, and the honest form of that answer is a table. Naming Bhakta on it would be a claim about writing that is not there -- the third time today I have caught the shape of stamping a register on a page nobody rewrote.
obs SO ONE OF THE THREE TOOK THE REGISTER RATHER THAN ALL THREE. study/README.md teaches a newcomer HOW TO READ this tree -- four questions, four rooms, two habits worth borrowing, and how to read a filename. That is teaching, which is what Bhakta is for. It carries the register now and grades 89 with a register of 86.
obs THE EDIT IT NEEDED WAS A WELCOME AND TWO SENTENCES, NOT A REWRITE. Its content was already plain and good. What it lacked was an opening that says this page assumes you have never read a codebase, and a line before the two habits saying they are the difference between reading this tree and trusting it.
obs AND THE BOUNDARY IS WRITTEN INTO THE ROOM THAT KEEPS GAUGE, WHICH IS THE PART THAT LASTS. edu/README.md now carries one paragraph saying why an index stays in Gauge and pointing at the two pages that teach. A ruling recorded only in a session log gets re-litigated; recorded in the room it rules on, it holds.
obs DEMOS I LEFT ALONE AND DID NOT DECIDE. It is four runnable things with verified outputs -- arguably Bhakta, arguably a reference card. Deciding it in the same lap that corrected my own three-page recommend would be repeating the error one page later.
loom bhakta_leaves named_by_me=3 genuinely_teaching=1 index_staying_gauge=1 undecided=1
loom qa study register_before=80 after=86 composite=89 reach_bhakta=9
file docs-geode/study/README.md the register taken, with a welcome and the habits framed
file docs-geode/edu/README.md the boundary written where it rules -- an index answers where, a teacher answers how
scope one Air lap -- three named leaves read, one taken, one ruled out in its own room, one left honestly undecided
status GREEN -- tracked links ok, ascii ok, study grading 89 at Door
recommend keep-going -- demos wants its own reading rather than my guess: run its four commands and see whether the page teaches or merely lists, and let that decide its register.
